+## Nested derived Debug builders (#1778)
+
+A derived Debug builder keeps its field coercions inside its own formatter.
+They are not values passed to an unrelated library writer. The written-parameter
+owner excludes those builder bodies from its foreign-dyn scan, as it already
+does for the initial dyn argument scan. Fields actually printed through a
+framed writer still enter through the existing field propagation path.
+The cross-crate regression includes a nested derived struct; its mutation
+restores scanning builder coercions and is caught. This preserves Rust behavior
+(ADR 0262, results change) without changing the separate explicit dyn boundary.
